// exp-arduino-s1.spec.vsm — first PHYSICAL S1: a two-photoresistor homeostat
// author [O] 2026-07-18 w/ rmw3. Device on n02 ✓. LOCKED gated past q4.
// PH-11 migrate + PH-11-CLOSE (2026-08-09): rewritten dense — prose ≤ 5%
// · w/l ≤ 5.0. Semantics preserved; compression real, ¬splitting.

spec(exp-arduino-s1) status=SPEC {

  purpose:
    "Minimal REAL/S1: closed homeostatic loop over light, genuine
     environmental variety (daily cycle). Nano sibling (ITEM_7) with real
     loop + physical input. Exercises external-S1 machinery (coupling,
     φ↑, S3* audit) in a SAFE, tiny physical system."

  device:
    "Arduino clone USB-serial CH340 (id 1a86:7523) → n02 /dev/ttyUSB0
     (ch341-uart, root:dialout). ✓ live 2026-07-18. Missing: exact
     FQBN/board (arduino-cli board list) + pins (2 ADC + 1 PWM LED)."

  the_S1:
    "HOMEOSTAT in firmware, AUTONOMOUS (D6: LLM ∉ L0/L1). Controlled: LED
     PWM. Measured: two photoresistors — ambient ∘ LED light. INVARIANT:
     |led_read − ambient_read| < ε; PWM regulates inside band while
     ambient drifts. State ≈ ℝ¹-ℝ² (nano-like). Disturbance = daily cycle ·
     regulation = LED adjust · viable = inside band."

  phi_up:
    "Serial telemetry each tick: {t, ambient, led, error=|led-ambient|,
     viable, pwm} — the φ↑. LXC reads serial, forwards to nucleus (any S1).
     Format aligned with CanonicalEvent, or LXC shim translates."

  roles_D6:
    "Firmware = S1 (autonomous). [O]: invariant + control law + firmware,
     audits φ↑. [S]: flashes (arduino-cli/avrdude), reads serial. [rmw3]:
     USB passthrough. Work WITH the Arduino as S3/S4 (design+audit), ¬as
     its control loop."

  infra:
    "1. Own TINY LXC (S1 = own crash-domain); s1-arduino.
     2. USB passthrough ttyUSB0 → LXC (edit /etc/pve/lxc/<id>.conf:
        devices.allow + mount). DELICATE — [rmw3] or reviewed change.
     3. Toolchain in LXC: arduino-cli/avrdude (flash) + pyserial (φ↑)."

  vsf_fit:
    "First PHYSICAL S1 with real variety (H0/H1 ladder). De-risks
     external-S1 like CLIMA, but physical. Proof: real loop, invariant,
     genuine φ↑, S3* auditing an uncontrolled S1. Agnosticism test #3."

  breaks:
    "not 'intelligence' — a light thermostat; the value = REAL physical loop +
     φ↑ + audit. ADC noise/drift: calibrate ε. LED photoresistor ISOLATED
     from ambient (else feedback trivial/unstable)."

  open_questions:
    "Q1 FQBN/board (verify on n02) · Q2 ADC/PWM pins · Q3 control law
     (proportional suffices) · Q4 baud + φ↑ format · Q5 optical isolation."

  gate:  "¬implement until q4 closes (nucleus). Order: spec → confirm
         device (board/pins) → LXC + passthrough → firmware v1
         (proportional) → flash → read φ↑ → couple to nucleus."
  owner: "design+firmware: [O] · flash+serial: [S] · passthrough: [rmw3]."
}

